  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1225 AM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nMoisture will stick around across the region from Labor Day into \nmuch of next week but does lower slightly more to near the 1.6 to \n1.9 inch range. Moisture will be highest, as typical, across the \nCoastal Plains closer to the coast. The moisture and a light to \nmoderate southeasterly low-level flow remains enough to promote \ndaily chances for isolated to scattered rain showers and storms \nacross the Coastal Plains, east of the I-35 corridor. Some of the \nlatest guidance picked up on the possibility for perhaps another \nweak inverted trough approaching from the Northern Gulf into late \nweek from Thursday through Friday. Right now, will elect to keep \nrain and storm chances mostly remain confined across the coastal \nplains through this period. The heat stays persistent with the \nafternoon highs in the mid to upper 90s with the heat indices \nhighest along/east of I-35 and across the Rio Grande Plains. The \nmorning lows hold in the 70s, with a few approaching 80 degrees at \ntimes.",
